# M4 walkthrough: the owner profile and department notes.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisite: a department with a lead (see m2-org.http) and a default model (m1-providers.http).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here
@departmentId = paste-a-department-id

### What the agents know about you (empty at first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Tell them. Every department agent gets a read-only copy on its next run.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sohaib",
  "language": "English",
  "communicationStyle": "Short and direct",
  "preferences": ["Use metric units", "Cite sources as links"]
}

### Remove a field with null
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "communicationStyle": null }

### The chief also learns as you talk (it updates the same profile)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agents/chief/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Note that I prefer answers in French from now on." }],
  "memory": { "thread": "chief:main", "resource": "owner" }
}

### A department's notes: rules and lessons its lead keeps across tasks
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/departments/{{departmentId}}/memory
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Correct them; the lead reads the new notes on its next task
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/departments/{{departmentId}}/memory
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "notes": "# Department notes\n- Rules and preferences from the owner: two sources per answer.\n" }
